'''Telugu literature''' includes poetry, short stories, novels, plays, and other works composed in [[Telugu language|Telugu]]. There is some indication that Telugu literature dates at least to the middle of the first millennium. The earliest extant works are from the 11th century when the [[Mahabharata]] was first translated to Telugu from Sanskrit by [[Nannaya]]. The language experienced a golden age under the patronage of the [[Vijayanagara Empire|Vijayanagara]] Emperor-Poet [[Krishnadevaraya]].{{Citation needed|date=November 2024}}

